   "text": "Our error in the definition of the pre-registered metric: with a spatially uniform wind every coastal station responds locally during the pulse (half-maximum reached at 2.0-3.7 h at 11 of 12 stations; pulse centre 2.5 h, sigma 1 h), so the first-arrival time measures the forced response, not a propagating Kelvin front, and c = 1.65 m/s is not a phase speed. Descriptive only (post hoc): lag of maximum correlation of the Kelvin-band displacement gives 0.64 m/s, with noisy lags.",
   "evidence": "figures/pd2_v2_diagnostics.json (post hoc)",
   "post_hoc_evidence": true,
   "pd2_decision": "Esteban, PD2 2026-11-13: verdict stays FAIL, class (a): the pre-registered front-arrival metric is not defined under spatially uniform forcing. Gill (2016) sec. 10.10, pp. 399-401, eq. 10.10.21 (thesis library Gill_2016 .md l.15449-15486): with a uniform wind of finite duration the coastal response is 1 - cos(pi t), independent of x, until the signal from the end of the coast arrives. Yao (1986), doi:10.1080/07055900.1986.9649249 (Yao_1986 .md l.553-558): the forced response has about half the free-wave alongshore phase gradient, so a free wave cannot be told from the forced response by phase alone.",
